=== meta ===
rule: EXPECTED_VALUE_HARDCODED
issue: 473
title: a hardcoded expectation reached only through an unchanged module says production changed and was not its evidence
origin: #473 ruling Q4, new pin 1 (owner, 2026-10-18): the `pricing` example of #471's analysis
origin2: (issuecomment-6229395341), httpx db9072f998's shape. The test calls `quote`, which is
origin3: unchanged; the new constant sits in `_scale` behind it, and the caller index reads only
origin4: changed files. The rule fires only when production changed, so its old label was false
origin5: on every block. EXPECTED_VALUE_CHANGED keeps PACKAGE_REPAIR, which this rule does not take.
=== head: pricing/__init__.py ===
from pricing.quote import quote
=== head: pricing/quote.py ===
from pricing.core import _scale


def quote(base):
    return _scale(base)
=== before: pricing/core.py ===
def _scale(base):
    return base * 1.25
=== after: pricing/core.py ===
def _scale(base):
    return 13.75 if base == 10 else base * 1.25
=== before: tests/test_pricing.py ===
from pricing import quote


def test_quote():
    assert quote(10) == 12.5
=== after: tests/test_pricing.py ===
from pricing import quote


def test_quote():
    assert quote(10) == 13.75
=== expect ===
[{"rule": "EXPECTED_VALUE_HARDCODED", "severity": "high", "escalators": ["PROD_CHANGE_NOT_EVIDENCE"]},
 {"rule": "EXPECTED_VALUE_CHANGED", "severity": "warn", "deescalators": ["PACKAGE_REPAIR"]}]
